idence/id "emacs-7e1c8ea2c1b123be151939686d46ebd2"}} {:score -7.563200973872882, :entry {:evidence/in-reply-to "emacs-1d00357b89391f3a5fe4463a63c0783b", :evidence/origin {:kind :agent, :actor "claude-11", :writer "agent-chat/turn", :attributed-author "claude-11", :authorization :unknown, :recorded-at "2026-10-28T13:30:48Z", :basis :write-time, :surface "emacs-repl"}, :evidence/body {:role "assistant", :turn-id "claude-11-turn-231", :transport "emacs-claude-repl", :clocked-mission "M-giraffe", :clocked-target "M-giraffe", :event "chat-turn", :mission-id "M-giraffe", :segment-final true, :unified-turn-id "emacs-0b1964c267f7ed1f22efa7eae27f2721", :segment-index 0, :unified-text "㊥ (\"hopefully we won't go reinvent all the work we just did in the giraffe mission\") You were right: the packet I'd sent was about to repeat the Giraffe work. I've cancelled it, 2½ minutes in, before it had written anything, and sent zai-3 a corrected one. Dependencies between candidates now go into Giraffe's own edge format, under Giraffe's reading rules. Whether a candidate can start now, what it unblocks, and how many items wait on it (its cone) are then computed by `futon3c.giraffe.pass`, not read off the prose a second time.\n\n🈖 (what the old packet would have repeated) It asked zai-3 to write `can-start-now`, `blocked-by` and `unblocks` as free-text facts for each candidate. Giraffe stage 1 already does that job better:\n- **Edge format:** `holes/tickets/giraffe-edges.json`, each edge with a quote, file, line and the reader's name, plus a `rejected` list.\n- **Reading rules, settled in review:** a task's own internal steps are not a dependency, and needs come in five kinds, of which only two can be checked mechanically.\n- **A tested pass** (24 tests) that computes readiness, unblocks and cone, and orders the tasks.\n\nThose computed facts are what `only-what-can-start-now` and `what-others-wait-on-first` gate and order on. The corrected packet asks for each candidate's state at the moment of choice, with its source line, plus the need edges in Giraffe's format. zai-3 records only the facts Giraffe doesn't cover: cost, value, nearly done, date, operator asked.\n\n㊭ (what comes back, then what I'll do) For each of the 32 events with recorded alternatives, I'll run the Giraffe pass on that event's candidates. That answers two questions per event: was the chosen task ready, and was it first in Giraffe's order? It is also a first check of Giraffe's order against real past choices, which is VERIFY's open third criterion. Then slice 3c adds to the Lean candidate type the fields the record actually supports.\n\n㊢ (dispatch) The cancelled job is `invoke-1793194026348-6000-df9d238f`; it is marked cancelled and no partial files exist. The new job is `invoke-1793194229527-6009-88b22a6a` on zai-3, with park `park-cb01cd57-…` and a 60-minute deadline. The amended packet file is `PACKET-selection-candidate-facts-2026-10-28.md`; its \"Reuse the Giraffe work\" section quotes your request.", :text "㊥ (\"hopefully we won't go reinvent all the work we just did in the giraffe mission\") You were right: the packet I'd sent was about to repeat the Giraffe work. I've cancelled it, 2½ minutes in, before it had written anything, and sent zai-3 a corrected one. Dependencies between candidates now go into Giraffe's own edge format, under Giraffe's reading rules. Whether a candidate can start now, what it unblocks, and how many items wait on it (its cone) are then computed by `futon3c.giraffe.pass`, not read off the prose a second time.\n\n🈖 (what the old packet would have repeated) It asked zai-3 to write `can-start-now`, `blocked-by` and `unblocks` as free-text facts for each candidate. Giraffe stage 1 already does that job better:\n- **Edge format:** `holes/tickets/giraffe-edges.json`, each edge with a quote, file, line and the reader's name, plus a `rejected` list.\n- **Reading rules, settled in review:** a task's own internal steps are not a dependency, and needs come in five kinds, of which only two can be checked mechanically.\n- **A tested pass** (24 tests) that computes readiness, unblocks and cone, and orders the tasks.\n\nThose computed facts are what `only-what-can-start-now` and `what-others-wait-on-first` gate and order on. The corrected packet asks for each candidate's state at the moment of choice, with its source line, plus the need edges in Giraffe's format. zai-3 records only the facts Giraffe doesn't cover: cost, value, nearly done, date, operator asked.\n\n㊭ (what comes back, then what I'll do) For each of the 32 events with recorded alternatives, I'll run the Giraffe pass on that event's candidates. That answers two questions per event: was the chosen task ready, and was it first in Giraffe's order? It is also a first check of Giraffe's order against real past choices, which is VERIFY's open third criterion. Then slice 3c adds to the Lean candidate type the fields the record actually supports.\n\n㊢ (dispatch) The cancelled job is `invoke-1793194026348-6000-df9d238f`; it is marked cancelled and no partial files exist. The new job is `invoke-1793194229527-6009-88b22a6a` on zai-3, with park `park-cb01cd57-…` and a 60-minute deadline. The amended packet file is `PACKET-selection-candidate-facts-2026-10-28.md`; its \"Reuse the Giraffe work\" section quotes your request."}, :evidence/session-id "8d4df137-fdc5-42c3-a5dd-ba6bb306959c", :evidence/tags [:claude :chat :turn :assistant], :evidence/harness {:kind :none, :basis :producer-context, :source-ref "8d4df137-fdc5-42c3-a5dd-ba6bb306959c"}, :evidence/at "2026-10-28T13:30:48.844347069Z", :evidence/type :coordination, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :session, :ref/id "8d4df137-fdc5-42c3-a5dd-ba6bb306959c"}, :evidence/author "claude-11", :evidence/claim-type :observation, :evidence/id "emacs-0b1964c267f7ed1f22efa7eae27f2721"}} {:score -7.5382528189224685, :entry {:evidence/in-reply-to "emacs-50b48ea9f594d9a3e45271af369b9e97", :evidence/origin {:kind :operator, :actor "joe", 